{
  "$comment": "Every FHIR package the HL7 FHIR validator loads in the gate (0005), each fetched from `url`, on packages.fhir.org, by exact version, and refused unless its SHA-256 is `sha256`. `loadedAs` says why: `core` is FHIR itself, which the gate names with -version; `ig` is a guide the gate asks for with -ig; `dependency` is one the validator loaded of its own accord. Which packages those are was read from the validator’s own load, its `Package Summary` line, never typed from a guide’s page. `declaredBy` is every registered package whose package.json declares this one at this version, `licence` and `canonical` what this one’s own package.json says, and `note` why a package no manifest declares is loaded. Read by scripts/validator.mjs and scripts/compatibility.mjs. Held by scripts/validator/registers.test.mjs, against the downloaded packages where they are present, and by scripts/validator.mjs in the validator job, which refuses a run that loaded a package this list does not name or did not load one it names. Read on 17 October 2026 from the bytes packages.fhir.org served, whose SHA-1 matched that registry’s own `dist.shasum` for every package.",
